// === Assembled-robot ROS2 demo — facet<->ROS2 binding (no hardware) ===
//
// Demonstrates wiring a DistanceSensor and a Motor to ROS2 topics using the
// Robotics facet library and the ros bridge, both running against the mock
// transport.  No ROS installation is required; the mock transport handles
// pub/sub in-process.
//
// Requires both URBI_ENABLE_ROS2=1 and URBI_ENABLE_UROBOTICS=1.
//
// Run with:
//   URBI_BUILD_PRESET=ros-urobotics build/host-ros-urobotics/urbi -i < examples/urobotics/ros_robot_demo.u

// ---- ROS2 node setup -----------------------------------------------------
ros.init("demo_bot");
cout << "ros node initialized";

// ---- Assemble the robot --------------------------------------------------
//
// A minimal single-sensor + single-motor robot.  Both facets are plain
// prototype clones; no hardware is involved.
var sensor = Robotics.DistanceSensor.clone();
sensor.distance = 1.0;

var motor = Robotics.Motor.clone();
motor.val = 1.0;

cout << "facets assembled";

// ---- Wire sensor input: /range -> sensor.distance -----------------------
//
// bindInput(facet, slot, topic, msgType, field)
//   Returns the underlying subscription Event.
//
// sensor_msgs/Range.range is float32.  The slot receives the float value
// on each incoming message.
var insub = Robotics.bindInput(sensor, "distance", "/range", "sensor_msgs/Range", "range");
cout << "sensor bound to /range";

// ---- Wire motor output: motor.val -> /cmd --------------------------------
//
// bindOutput(facet, slot, topic, msgType, field, rate)
//   Returns a handle with a publishNow() method.
//   rate = 100ms: installs every(100ms) publishNow() automatically.
//   rate = 0ms:   on-demand only — call publishNow() explicitly.
//
// motor.val is a Float64-backed slot.  Assign FLOAT literals (1.0, 0.0) so
// the value marshals correctly; an integer literal in a Float64 field will
// produce an incorrect wire value.
var out = Robotics.bindOutput(motor, "val", "/cmd", "std_msgs/Float64", "data", 100ms);
cout << "motor bound to /cmd (100ms periodic)";

// ---- Reactive safety behavior --------------------------------------------
//
// When the sensor reads closer than 0.5 m the motor stops immediately.
// The at-watcher fires each time sensor.distance crosses below 0.5; the
// motor slot update is picked up by the next periodic publish cycle.
at (sensor.distance < 0.5) motor.val = 0.0;
cout << "safety behavior installed";

cout << "demo running";
motor.val;
sensor.distance;

// ---- Expected behavior ---------------------------------------------------
//
// With a real ROS2 DDS transport:
//   - /cmd receives std_msgs/Float64 { data: 1.0 } every 100 ms.
//   - When a sensor_msgs/Range message arrives on /range with range < 0.5,
//     sensor.distance updates, the at-watcher sets motor.val = 0.0, and the
//     next /cmd publish carries { data: 0.0 }.
//
// With the mock transport (this demo):
//   - bindOutput installs the periodic publisher; publishNow() is available
//     for on-demand testing.
//   - Inject a message via ros.__injectMsg to exercise the full pipeline.

cout << "demo complete";
